358	//! places HDR10 static metadata lives, from bytes Swift hands it, so import
359	//! reads one answer whatever wrote the file. Reached through `rc_hdr10_peak`
360	//! (`ffi_hdr10.rs`); what the answer becomes on the media is
361	//! `media_color.rs`'s.
362	//!
363	//! - **The sample description** (what Apple's writer stores, and the only
364	//!   place AVFoundation reads): the `MasteringDisplayColorVolume` extension,
365	//!   24 bytes of SMPTE ST 2086 in the order H.265's SEI 137 carries them —
366	//!   three primaries and the white point as u16 pairs, then the maximum and
367	//!   minimum luminance as big-endian u32 in 0.0001 cd/m² (the maximum at
368	//!   bytes 16–19) — and the `ContentLightLevelInfo` extension, 4 bytes of
369	//!   CTA-861.3: MaxCLL then MaxFALL, big-endian u16 cd/m².
370	//! - **The HEVC stream** (where ffmpeg, HandBrake and x265 write it): the
371	//!   first sample's length-prefixed NAL units, the prefix SEI units (type 39)
372	//!   before its first VCL unit (type below 32), their emulation-prevention
373	//!   bytes removed, each `sei_message`'s `ff`-extended type and size
374	//!   (ITU-T H.265 §7.3.5), payloads 137 (`mastering_display_colour_volume`,
375	//!   the same 24 bytes) and 144 (`content_light_level_info`, the same 4).
376	//!
377	//! - **The AV1 stream** (spec §11 HD-18 (c); AV1 §5.3, §5.8, §6.7;
378	//!   AV1-ISOBMFF §2.3): the `av1C` record's configOBUs (bytes 4 on, when its
379	//!   first byte is 0x81, the marker and version 1), then the first sample's
380	//!   OBUs — each OBU's type in its header's bits 6–3, an extension byte
381	//!   skipped, its leb128 `obu_size` when it has one, else the rest of the
382	//!   bytes — and in each OBU_METADATA (type 5) its leb128 `metadata_type`:
383	//!   HDR_CLL (1; `max_cll` then `max_fall`, CTA-861.3's 4 bytes) and
384	//!   HDR_MDCV (2; ST 2086's 24 bytes, but `luminance_max` in 24.8 fixed
385	//!   point), the first of each kept, the config's first. Reached through
386	//!   `rc_hdr10_av1_peak` for an `av01` track whose description carries
387	//! A PQ still's HDR10 peak (spec §11 HD-20 (b)): a pure reader of the two
388	//! places a still image carries HDR10 static metadata, from the file's bytes
389	//! Swift hands it, so import reads a PQ PNG, HEIF or AVIF as it reads a PQ
390	//! video (`hdr10.rs`, whose arithmetic and choice it shares). Reached through
391	//! `rc_hdr10_still_peak` (`ffi_hdr10.rs`); what the answer becomes on the
392	//! media is `media_color.rs`'s.
393	//!
394	//! - **PNG** (W3C PNG third edition §11.3.2.7, §11.3.2.8): the chunks before
395	//!   the first `IDAT`, the first `cLLI` (8 bytes or more; MaxCLL a
396	//!   big-endian u32 in 0.0001 cd/m², then MaxFALL) and the first `mDCV` (24
397	//!   bytes or more; ST 2086's order, its maximum luminance a big-endian u32
398	//!   in 0.0001 cd/m² at bytes 16–19). CRCs are not checked.
399	//! - **ISOBMFF** (HEIF and AVIF, `ftyp` at bytes 4–8; ISO/IEC 23008-12
400	//!   §9.3): the first top-level `meta` (a FullBox) gives its `pitm` (the
401	//!   primary item's id, a u16 at version 0, else a u32) and its `iprp`,
402	//!   whose `ipco` holds the properties (1-based) and whose `ipma` (a FullBox)
403	//!   the associations: an entry's item id a u16 at version 0, else a u32; a
404	//!   u8 `association_count`; each association a u16 when `flags & 1`, else
405	//!   a u8, its index the low 15 or low 7 bits. Among the primary item's
406	//!   properties, the first `clli` (4 bytes or more, CTA-861.3's MaxCLL) and
407	//!   the first `mdcv` (24 bytes or more, ST 2086). A box size of 1 means a
408	//!   64-bit size follows, 0 that the box runs to its parent's end, and a box
